            <ArticleTitle>Facial neuralgias: a clinical review of 34 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>752-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper reviewed the clinical features of the facial neuralgias, and described the demographic data for 24 cases of atypical facial neuralgia, seven cases of trigeminal neuralgia, two cases of cluster headache and one of glossopharyngeal neuralgia, which were all referred for investigation and treatment over a three-month period to a teaching hospital dental department.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
